DNS resolves the domain name to an IP address, TCP establishes a connection, TLS secures it (if HTTPS), and HTTP is used to request and receive data from the server, which the browser then renders.
DNS is the system that resolves human-readable domain names into machine-readable IP addresses through a multi-step hierarchical lookup process.
